---
const highlights = [
  { value: "10+", label: "studios adopted the platform" },
  { value: "2017", label: "founded as sole product owner" },
  { value: "Ongoing", label: "still owned for a flagship studio" },
];
---

<section id="achievement" class="mesh-bg px-6 py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-5 md:gap-16">
    <div class="reveal md:col-span-3">
      <h2 class="eyebrow text-xs font-semibold uppercase text-[#a9791f] mb-3">Signature Work</h2>
      <h3 class="font-serif-heading text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#111827] leading-snug">
        Operational CRM Platform — Back-Office Automation for Live-Ops Gaming
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-6 text-[#5b6472] leading-relaxed">
        Owned the end-to-end product for a back-office CRM system supporting live
        operations across a mobile gaming organization, from 2017 through its
        evolution from a single monolithic platform into a distributed model
        adopted by 10+ independent studios.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[#5b6472] leading-relaxed">
        As the product's original owner, I defined the core configuration
        architecture — UI/UX for the configuration modules, the underlying file
        structure, and asset management — decisions that shaped how safely and
        quickly operational teams could ship changes to production. When the
        platform split from a single shared system into studio-specific
        instances, I stayed on as owner for one of the largest studios while
        supporting other teams through their onboarding, effectively acting as
        the product's institutional memory during a major architectural
        transition.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[#5b6472] leading-relaxed">
        The system's value compounds directly with its adoption: every
        configuration workflow it automates removes a manual, error-prone step
        from day-to-day operations — reducing production downtime, minimizing
        configuration mistakes that reach live environments, and cutting the
        operational load on teams managing customer-facing features. Long-term
        ownership of a platform this central to daily operations meant
        balancing UX simplicity for non-technical operators against the
        flexibility power users needed — a tension I navigated continuously as
        the product matured.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal md:col-span-2 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 content-start sm:grid-cols-3 sm:gap-4 md:grid-cols-1">
      {highlights.map((item) => (
        <div class="card-elevate card-sheen spotlight rounded-xl border border-[#e3e6ec] bg-white p-5">
          <div class="font-serif-heading text-3xl text-[#0f3d68]">{item.value}</div>
          <div class="mt-1 text-sm text-[#5b6472]">{item.label}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
